(:probe "actual-in-tool-discovery" :value (:contract_version "1" :tools ("bash" "edit-file" "glob" "grep" "read-file" "write-file") :result_contract (:tool_results "ogent-agent-call returns versioned status/data/error/next envelopes; legacy functions default to text" :schema "(ogent-agent-schema 'json)" :continuation "(ogent-agent-next RESULT) follows the next page and guards snapshots" :batch "ogent-agent-batch accepts up to 20 declared read-only calls" :async_sdk "ogent-agent-call-async returns a process and invokes one terminal callback" :async_events ["stdout" "stderr" "done" "error"] :doctor_exit_codes (:ok 0 :warning 1 :error 2)) :guide "ogent agent guide (contract 1)
Load ogent normally, then inspect (ogent-agent-capabilities 'json).
This reads the live registry; an empty tools array means no tools are installed.
(ogent-tools-install-defaults) explicitly installs built-in specs if wanted.
Use canonical hyphen names or registered underscore aliases; typos get hints, never execution.
Use (ogent-agent-describe \"read\" 'json) for exact call_arguments and examples.
Call (ogent-agent-call \"read\" '(:file_path \"README.org\" :limit 40) 'json).
Named calls reject unknown/duplicate keys before approval.
Native boolean false is nil or :json-false; zero and nested objects are preserved.
MCP calls use :json-false for explicit false; optional nil means omit the argument.
Named calls return contract_version 1, tool, status, data, error and next.
Status ok means success, even for empty files or no matches; error includes code/message/recovery.
Legacy ogent-tool-- functions still default to text; optional plist/json selects structured data.
Read data: lines[number,column,text,partial], content, ends_with_newline, total_lines, snapshot.
Glob data: files[path,size,modified], total_files and snapshot; stable path ordering.
Search data: matches[path,line,text,context_before,context_after,truncated], total_matches and snapshot.
Search text can be truncated while retaining every returned match's path and line.
Read offsets/columns start at 1; search/glob offsets start at 0. Follow (ogent-agent-next RESULT).
Continuations freeze absolute targets and refuse changed snapshots. Do not combine different snapshots.
A long read line continues at its exact column, retaining all characters over successive pages.
Search pages cap at 200 matches and context at 20 lines; GNU fallback uses ERE syntax.
(ogent-agent-batch '[(:tool \"files\" :args (:pattern \"**/*.el\")) (:tool \"read\" :args (:file_path \"README.org\"))]) batches reads only.
(ogent-agent-call-async \"shell\" '(:command \"pwd\") #'YOUR-CALLBACK) returns a process with one terminal result.
Cancel that process with ogent-tool-process-cancel; timeout/cancel retains partial output.
(ogent-agent-schema 'json) exports the result envelope JSON Schema.
Read: (ogent-tool--read-file \"/path/file\" 1 200); follow the exact next offset in its footer.
Search: (ogent-tool--glob \"**/*.el\" \"/path/project\") includes every depth.
Grep: (ogent-tool--grep \"-needle\" \"/path/project\"); no matches is success, invalid regex is an error.
Edit: old_string must be nonempty and unique; set replace_all to t only for intentional repeated replacement.
Read-only tools need no confirmation by default. Writes and shell execution require approval.
Programmatic calls never prompt or grant approval: approval_required directs you to the user review flow.
Direct ogent-tool-- functions are low-level APIs; use registered execution wrappers for approval enforcement.
Shell: use a positive timeout in seconds and an existing working_directory.
Shell stdout/stderr may be truncated; the final exit code is preserved.
Structured shell data has stdout, stderr, exit_code, signal, timed_out, cancelled and truncated.
Nonzero exits have status error; inspect retained data. encoding_loss marks UTF-8 replacements.
Local health: (ogent-agent-triage 'json), no provider requests or MCP handshakes.
Batch health: (ogent-doctor-batch nil 'json), exit 0=ok/info, 1=warning, 2=error.
Check readiness offline: make test; make test-isolation; make offline-test with OGENT_ELPA_DIR.
Build/test reports: make test format=json; make lint format=json. Diagnostics stay on stderr.
Discover actual build tasks and exits: ./makem.sh --capabilities --json.
"))
